                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000053"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The cell cortex specifically associated with the vegetal hemisphere of an oocyte or a zygote.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000102</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>vegetal cortex</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000103 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000103">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000003"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000052"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The most apical region of the animal hemisphere. Among echinoderms, in euechinoids, it is characterized by the presence of long, immotile cilia constituting the apical tuft initially and then, in all echinoderms, by te presence of the oral hood and where the serotonergic neurons form.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000103</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>animal pole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000104 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000104">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000003"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000053"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The most apical region of the vegetal hemisphere. Among echinoderms, in euechinoids, once cleavages have started, the vegetal pole is characterized by the presence of the micromeres initially and then that of the small micromeres. Subsequently, it is marked by the site of ingression of the primary mesenchyme cells (PMCs), and finally in all echinoderms by the site of invagination and presence of the blastopore.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000104</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>vegetal pole</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000105 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000105">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000003"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000008"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The middle region of an oocyte or a zygote, which comprises the most basal portion of the animal and vegetal hemispheres.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>equator</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000105</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>equator region</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000106 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000106">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000053"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An accumulation of pigment granules defining a band (the so-called ‘pigment band’) located in the vegetal hemisphere of mature oocytes or early stage embryos just beneath the equator. When present, it constitutes an unambiguous marker of animal-vegetal polarity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>pigment band</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>pigmented band</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000106</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>equatorial pigment band</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000107 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000107">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000008"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A structure that lies outside the plasma membrane and surrounds the fertilized eggs and early embryos. The fertilization envelope forms from the vitelline membrane after fertilization as a result of cortical granule release. It persists until hatching.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0060387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>fertilization membrane</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000107</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>fertilization envelope</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000108 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000108">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000065"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A structure directly adjacent to the outer surface of the plasma membrane of an ovum. It is composed mostly of protein fibers, with protein receptors needed for sperm binding. The species-specificity of these receptors contributes to prevention of breeding between different species.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0060388</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>vitelline envelope</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>vitelline layer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000108</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>vitelline membrane</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000109 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000109">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000116"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A secretory vesicle that is stored under the cell membrane of an egg. These vesicles fuse with the egg plasma membrane as part of egg activation and are part of the block to polyspermy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0060473</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cortical vesicle</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000109</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>cortical granule</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000110 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000110">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000088"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An array of microtubules arranged radially that emanates from a spindle pole and is not connect to kinetochores.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0005818</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>mitotic aster</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spindle aster</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000110</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>aster</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000111 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000111">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000131"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multisubunit complex that is located on chromosomes and provides an attachment point for the spindle microtubules.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0000776</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000111</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>kinetochore</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000112 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000112">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000006"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A structure lying external to one or more cells, which provides structural support, biochemical or biomechanical cues for cells or tissues.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0031012</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000112</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>extracellular matrix</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000113 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000113">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000112"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multilayered extraembryonic matrix that functions as a substrate for cell adhesion through early development. It forms initially from molecules secreted from cortical granules at fertilization and is modified through the secretion of additional material during later development. The principal component of the hyaline layer is the protein, hyalin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0033166</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>hyaline membrane</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000113</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>hyaline layer</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000114 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000114">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000113"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A fibrous, extracellular network that forms the inner part of the hyaline layer. The apical lamina persists after the biochemical removal of hyalin and is thought to be principally composed of the glycoproteins fibropellins.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0032579</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>fibropellin layer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000114</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>apical lamina</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000115 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000115">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A thin cylindrical membrane-covered projection on the surface of a cell containing a core bundle of actin filaments.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0005902</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000115</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>microvillus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000116 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000116">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000095"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cytoplasmic, membrane bound vesicle that is capable of fusing to the plasma membrane and to release its contents into the extracellular space.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0099503</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000116</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>secretory vesicle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000117 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000117">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A specialized organelle that consists of a filiform extrusion of the cell surface and of some cytoplasmic parts. Each cilium is largely bounded by an extrusion of the cytoplasmic (plasma) membrane, and contains a regular longitudinal array of microtubules, anchored to a basal body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0005929</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>flagellum</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000117</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>cilium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000118 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000118">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000117"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000006"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cilium that develops on the apical surface of a cell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000118</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>apical cilium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000119 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000119">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000117"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000013"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cilium of short size exhibiting motility thanks to the molecular motors it contains. In echinoderms, short motile cilia are encountered on the outer surface of the developing embryo as well as in the developing and developed digestive tract of embryos and larvae.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0031514</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000119</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>short motile cilium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000120 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000120">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000117"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000227"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cilium of long size that does not contain molecular motors and as such does not exhibit any beating movement. In some echinoderms, long immotile cilia are found, when present, at the animal pole of embryos and constitute the apical tuft.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0097730</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>elongated cilium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>long non-motile cilium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000120</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>long immotile cilium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000121 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000121">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A thin, stiff, actin-based protrusion extended by the leading edge of a motile cell such as an ingressing or crawling mesenchyme cell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0030175</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>pseudopod</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000121</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>filopodium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000122 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000122">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sheet-like cellular projection that is supported by an ordered network of actin filaments and that is involved in cellular motility and syncytium formation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C32914</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>lamellipodia</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000122</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>filopodial cable</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000123 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000123">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000080"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An acellular anatomical structure that consists of a thin sheet of fibrous proteins that underlie and support the cells of an epithelium. It separates the cells of an epithelium from any underlying tissue.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UBERON:0000482</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000123</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>basal lamina</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000124 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000124">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000116"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A secretory vesicle containing molecules that will be secreted and incorporated into the basal lamina.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>basal lamina vesicle</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>basal vesicle</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000124</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>basal laminar vesicle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000125 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000125">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000116"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A secretory vesicle found near the outer (apical) surface of an oocyte, a spermatozoid head, or an early blastomere, and that contains molecules that will be incorporated into the hyaline layer after secretion.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000125</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>apical vesicle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000126 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000126">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000116"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A secretory vesicle that contains echinonectin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EN-vesicle</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>echinonectin granule</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>nectosome</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000126</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>echinonectin vesicle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000127 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000127">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000095"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A semiautonomous, self-replicating organelle that occurs in varying numbers, shapes, and sizes in the cytoplasm of the cells. It is notably the site of tissue respiration.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0005739</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>mitochondria</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000127</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>mitochondrion</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000128 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000128">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000093"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The portion of the nuclear content that is not the chromosomes or the nucleolus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0005654</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000128</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>nucleoplasm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000129 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000129">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000093"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A double lipid bilayer enclosing the nucleus and separating its contents from the rest of the cytoplasm.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0005635</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000129</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>nuclear envelope</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000130 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000130">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000081"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000093"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A small, dense body present in the nucleus of cells and that is rich in RNA and protein, not bounded by a limiting membrane, and not seen during mitosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GO:0005730</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000130</oboInOwl:id>
