            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The layer of cells that form the archenteron, but at the level of its anterior tip and that of the blastopore.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000496</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>archenteron wall</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000497 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000497">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000026"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000494"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The orifice of invagination of the endomesodermal cells during the embryonic stages of an organism. The opening of the archenteron to the exterior, which will later develop into the larval anus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UBERON:0000100</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000497</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>blastopore</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000498 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000498">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000001"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000497"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The margin (or edge) of the blastopore. In echinoderms, it is the circular rim of the blastopore and the transition zone between the invaginated archenteron and the outer epithelium of the embryo. Because cells move over the lip of the blastopore during echinoderm gastrulation, different populations of cells are located at the blastopore lip as gastrulation proceeds.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UBERON:3010455</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>rim of blastopore</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000498</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>blastopore lip</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


