        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>subequatorial SM ring</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>subequatorial primary mesenchyme cell ring</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000562</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>subequatorial skeletogenic mesenchyme ring</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000563 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000563">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000026"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000555"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000562"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A straight, syncitial network that either links the two ventrolateral skeletogenic mesenchyme clusters within the subequatorial skeletogenic mesenchyme ring or extends from the ventrolateral skeletogenic mesenchyme clusters towards the animal pole domain.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000563</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000564 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000564">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000563"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell that within the subequatorial skeletogenic mesenchyme ring links the two ventrolateral skeletogenic mesenchyme clusters on the oral side of the embryo. The ventral transverse rods will be deposited along this cellular strand.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>oral chain of PMCs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ventral chain of PMCs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ventral skeletogenic mesenchyme chain</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000564</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>oral chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000565 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000565">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000563"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell that within the subequatorial skeletogenic mesenchyme ring links the two ventrolateral skeletogenic mesenchyme clusters on the aboral side of the embryo. The body rods will be deposited along this cellular strand.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>aboral chain of PMCs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>dorsal chain of PMCs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>dorsal skeletogenic mesenchyme chain</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000565</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>aboral chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000566 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000566">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000001"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000006"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cluster of skeletogenic mesenchyme cells that aggregates before any calcification event whether in the embryo, the larva, or the adult.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000566</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>skeletogenic mesenchyme cluster</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000567 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000567">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000026"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000555"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000562"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A skeletogenic mesenchyme cluster that forms in the ventrolateral region of the subequatorial skeletogenic mesenchyme ring of an embryo and will be the seat of a triradiate spicule rudiment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ventrolateral cluster</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ventrolateral cluster of skeletogenic mesenchyme cells</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000567</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>ventrolateral skeletogenic mesenchyme cluster</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000568 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000568">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000567"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A skeletogenic mesenchyme cluster that forms in the right, ventrolateral region of the embryo.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000568</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>right ventrolateral skeletogenic mesenchyme cluster</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000569 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000569">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000567"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A skeletogenic mesenchyme cluster that forms in the left, ventrolateral region of the embryo.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000569</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>left ventrolateral skeletogenic mesenchyme cluster</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000570 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000570">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000563"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000556"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000561"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell that extends from a ventrolateral cluster toward the animal pole. A dorsoventral connecting rod will be deposited along this cellular strand.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>lateral chain of PMCs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000570</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>lateral chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000571 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000571">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000570"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The lateral chain that forms on the right side of the embryo from the right ventrolateral cluster.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>right lateral chain of PMCs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000571</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>right lateral chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000572 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000572">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000570"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The lateral chain that forms on the left side of the embryo from the left ventrolateral cluster.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>left lateral chain of PMCs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000572</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>left lateral chain of skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000573 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000573">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000049"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A very small, punctate deposit of calcite; i.e., the biomineralized primordium for spicule formation. It will undergo growth and often branching to produce a complex skeletal element.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>amorphous calcium carbonate-containing granule</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>rhombohedral calcite crystal</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>rhombohedral crystal</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>small granules of calcite</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spicule crystal</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spicule dot</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spicule primordium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spicule rudiment</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000573</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>spicule granule</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000574 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000574">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000049"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000573"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A skeletal, calcified structure composed of three short radii extending from a central point, the radii being separated by angles of 120 degrees.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>spicule rudiment</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>triradiate element with elongating skeletal rods</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000574</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>triradiate spicule rudiment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000575 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000575">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000049"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000574"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A skeletal, calcified structure composed of three elongated skeletal rods.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>triradiate element</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000575</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>triradiate spicule</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000576 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000576">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000573"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000567"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000046"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A spicule granule that forms within a ventrolateral cluster of skeletogenic mesenchyme cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000576</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>ventrolateral spicule granule</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000577 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000577">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000576"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000568"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ventrolateral spicule granule that forms on the right side of the embryo.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000577</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>right ventrolateral spicule granule</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000578 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000578">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000576"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000569"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ventrolateral spicule granule that forms on the left side of the embryo.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000578</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>left ventrolateral spicule granule</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000579 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000579">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000574"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000576"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000046"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A triradiate spicule rudiment that forms within a ventrolateral cluster of skeletogenic mesenchyme cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000579</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>ventrolateral triradiate spicule rudiment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000580 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000580">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000579"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000577"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ventrolateral triradiate spicule rudiment that forms on the right side of embryo. This rudiment elongates its radii between the vegetal pole and the equator of the embryo along and away from the oral wall of the blastocoel.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000580</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>right ventrolateral triradiate spicule rudiment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000581 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000581">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000579"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000578"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ventrolateral triradiate spicule rudiment that forms on the left side of embryo. This rudiment elongates its radii between the vegetal pole and the equator of the embryo along and away from the oral wall of the blastocoel.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000581</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>left ventrolateral triradiate spicule rudiment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000546"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000547"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An embryonic, larval or adult region that will develop into non-skeletogenic mesoderm and/or mesenchyme derivatives.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000582</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000583 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000583">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000547"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The subset of the mesoderm germ layer that will give rise to all mesoderm tissue derivatives but the endoskeleton; e.g. muscles, coeloms, pigment cells, blastocoelar cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000583</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>non-skeletogenic mesoderm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000584 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000584">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000058"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000583"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cell part of the mesoderm germ layer subset that will give rise to all mesoderm tissue derivatives but the endoskeleton; e.g. muscles, coeloms, pigment cells, blastocoelar cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000584</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>non-skeletogenic mesoderm cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000585 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000585">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000548"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000583"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>All mesenchyme present in the embryo, larva, or adult but that does not constitute the endoskeleton.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000585</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>non-skeletogenic mesenchyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000586 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000586">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000058"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000548"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A mesenchymal cell that participates in the elaboration of all mesenchyme derivatives but the endoskeleton; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000586</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000587 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000587">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000153"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm that derives from the vegetal 2 tier cells and not from the small micromere descendants.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000587</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>vegetal tier 2 non-skeletogenic mesoderm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000588 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000588">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000585"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000008"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The non-skeletogenic mesenchyme that is present in an embryo.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>secondary mesenchyme</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000588</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>embryonic non-skeletogenic mesenchyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000589 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000589">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000586"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000588"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An embryonic cell that after undergoing an epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition in present in the blastocoel and will give rise to a non-skeletogenic mesenchyme derivative; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells, globular cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SMC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>secondary mesenchyme cell</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000589</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>embryonic non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000590 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000590">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000585"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000012"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The non-skeletogenic mesenchyme that is present in a larva.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000590</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>larval non-skeletogenic mesenchyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000591 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000591">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000586"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000590"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A larval cell that present in the blastocoel and participating in a non-skeletogenic mesenchyme derivative; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells, globular cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000591</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>larval non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000592 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000592">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000549"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000008"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In echinoderms with no embryonic endoskeleton, all embryonic cells that have undergone an epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition and will participate in the elaboration of non-skeletogenic mesoderm derivatives; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000592</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>embryonic mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000593 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000593">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000549"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000012"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In echinoderms with no larval endoskeleton, all larval mesenchyme cells that participate in the elaboration of non-skeletogenic mesoderm derivatives; e.g. pigment cells, blastocoelar cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000593</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>larval mesenchyme cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000594 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000594">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000053"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm that in the vegetal plate is on the oral side of the embryo.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>oral non-skeletogenic mesoderm</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ventral non-skeletogenic mesoderm</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ventral presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000594</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>oral presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000595 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000595">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000053"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm that in the vegetal plate is on the aboral side of the embryo.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>aboral non-skeletogenic mesoderm</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>dorsal non-skeletogenic mesoderm</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>dorsal presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000595</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>aboral presumptive non-skeletogenic mesoderm</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000596 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000596">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000594"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cell that within the oral presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm will give rise to a blastocoelar cell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000596</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>presumptive blastocoelar cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000597 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000597">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000582"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000595"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cell that within the aboral presumptive embryonic non-skeletogenic mesoderm will give rise to a pigment cell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>presumptive immunocyte</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>presumptive pigmented cell</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000597</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>presumptive pigment cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000598 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000598">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000549"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000032"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cell of the immune system that is involved in protecting the body against infectious disease and foreign invaders.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>immunocyte</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000598</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>immune cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000598"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000596"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A class of migratory, non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell, fibroblastic in appearance, which secrete extracellular matrix and exert immune cell functions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000599</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>blastocoelar cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000600 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000600">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000598"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000597"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A class of migratory, non-skeletogenic mesenchyme cell that produces visible pigment, usually reddish, and exert immune cell functions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CL:0000147</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000600</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>pigment cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000601 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000601">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000034"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A subclass of blastocoelar cells; 10–15 μm in diameter, filled with large, flattened vesicles, and expressing a perforin-like marker (macpfA2).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000601</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>globular cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000602 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000602">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000034"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A heterogeneous subclass of blastocoelar cells; 5–7 μm in diameter, and with 2 to 5 filopodial projections that extend 10–50 μm. Filopodial cells are located in the blastocoel and across the basal surface of ectoderm and gut epithelia, and form multiple interconnected, syncytial networks.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000602</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>filopodial cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000603 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000603">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000602"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The subset of the filopodial cells that are phagocytic and express the immune effector gene 185/333.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000603</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>phagocytic filopodial cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000604 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000604">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000034"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A subclass of blastoceolar cells; 10–15 μm on their longest axis,  granular, oval-shaped, and non-syncytial. Ovoid cells arise in the blastocoel under some conditions of immune challenge, possibly from a morphological transformation of filopodial cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000604</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>ovoid cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000605 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000605">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000599"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000034"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A subclass of blastocoelar cells; 5-10 μm in size and comma-shaped. They are distinguishable by their rapid migration within the blastocoel and to sites of bacterial exposure.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CL:0000732</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000605</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>amoeboid cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000606 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000606">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000584"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000492"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000008"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cell present in the embryo that has the potential to give rise to a muscle cell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CL:0000680</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>muscle precursor cell</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000606</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>presumptive muscle cell</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000607 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000607">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000021"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000547"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000043"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The contractile tissue of an animal that is derived from mesoderm and contracts when stimulated thereby producing movement.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UBERON:0001630</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>muscle organ</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>ECAO:2000607</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>muscle</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000608 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000608">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000584"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecao#develops_from"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000606"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
